<div id="2026-11-06-restock-levels" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-06 — replenishment is driven by the container's minimum, and stock moves before it prints</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> New table <code>inventory_location_levels</code> (item + location → min_level, max_level) sets a minimum per container. Applying a count now replenishes the container to <em>its own minimum</em>, not to the count's shortfall: it takes surplus from other containers first (a transfer — two <code>inventory_transactions</code> rows, <code>transfer_out</code>/<code>transfer_in</code>, no GL, total unchanged), and only what cannot be pulled is queued as print jobs (for <code>3d_printed</code> items) or reported as an order need (bought items). <code>inventory_consignments.invoice_id</code> added so a batch cites its invoice directly.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The old top-up fired on <code>expected − counted</code>, so a perfectly correct count left a container below its minimum with no work raised, and stock that already existed elsewhere was printed again instead of moved.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>The rule.</strong> Only an invoice removes stock; a consignment form moves it between locations and records delivery. Direct sale and consignment sale are the same event for stock. Min is per container, stock level is the sum of containers.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Verified</strong> in a rolled-back transaction: item 41 with min 5, coop container at 4 after the count, warehouse at 6 → surplus 1 pulled (warehouse settled at its own min 5, coop at 5), two transfer rows written, zero print jobs. Total on hand unchanged.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Not yet.</strong> Sale invoices do not remove stock anywhere in the codebase today — the invoice path needs that removal before it can call the same helper. Until then the shared path is used by the count/consignment apply.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Schema to apply.</strong> Create <code>inventory_location_levels</code>, add <code>inventory_consignments.invoice_id</code> (Update Table on the schema-compare page).</p>
</div>
